      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “ototoxic” as a general term meaning “damaging effect on the inner ear”; it only uses “ototoxic exposure” as a described experimental condition.",
        "Although the packet reports histological changes in the utricle and cochlear alterations after “ototoxic exposure,” it does not explicitly state that this corresponds to “balance-related” versus “hearing-related” parts of the ear.",
